$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Step 1. A mixture of the commercially
available phenol (3.0 mmol) (59 a-d), 4-fluoro-3-methoxybenzonitrile
(0.47 g, 6.0 mmol) in DMSO (4.0 mL) and anhydrous K2CO3 (0.62 g, 4.5
mmol) was heated at 130°C for 5 h. The reaction mixture was poured into
ice water and extracted with EtOAc (3 × 50 mL). The organic layer was
sequentially washed with brine (2 × 75 mL), dried over anhydrous Na2SO4,
and concentrated in vacuo. The residue was purified by column
chromatography. 4-(3,5-dichlorophenoxy)-3-methoxybenzonitrile (60d):
yield (0.88 g, 100%). 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3) δ 7.40 (d, J= 1.5Hz, 1H),
7.31 - 7.20 (m, 2H), 7.18 (dd, J= 1.31, 2.33 Hz, 1H), 6.94 - 6.77 (m,
2H), 3.83 (s, 3H). 13C NMR (126 MHz, CDCl3) δ 152.05, 150.58, 147.00,
133.34, 131.51, 125.95, 125.87, 125.41, 123.77, 120.12, 118.46, 116.73,
108.25, 49.91.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
