$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM To a solution of N-BOC 4-fluorophenylsulfone ethyl ester 15 42 (1.5 g,
3.61 mmol) in DMF (10 mL) was added Cs2CO3 (2.94 g, 9.03 mmol) and
4-(trifluoromethoxy)- phenol (0.70 mL, 5.41 mmol). The solution was
heated to 90 °C for 20 h. The solution was then cooled and partitioned
between EtOAc and water, and the organic layer was washed with brine and
dried over Na2SO4. Filtration through a pad of silica gel eluting with
EtOAc provided the diaryl ether 16u as a yellow oil (2.11 g, 100%).
MS(CI) MNa+ calcd for C26H30F3NO8S, 596; found, 596.
