$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Step 2. A mixture of 68 (0.8 g, 5.4 mmol), 2,5-dichlorophenol (59 c)
(0.98 g, 6.0 mmol) in DMSO (10.0 mL) and anhydrous K2CO3 (1.12 g, 8.1
mmol) was heated at 50°C for 4 h. The mixture was poured into ice water
extracted with EtOAc (3 × 50 mL). The organic layer was sequentially
washed with brine (2 × 75 mL), dried over anhydrous Na2SO4, and
concentrated in vacuo. The residue was purified by column chromatography.
65 (1.40 g, 100%). 1H NMR (500 MHz, CDCl3) δ 10.30 (s, 1H), 8.40 (d, J=
2.7 Hz, 1H), 8.12 (d, J= 7.9 Hz, 1H), 7.74 (m, 2H), 7.30 (d, J= 8.7, 1H),
7.24 (s, 1H). HR-MS (ES) calcd for C14H7Cl2NO2 [M+1]+ 293.0100, found
293.0102.
