$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM To a solution of 20 (1.26 g, 4.54mmol) in DMF (40 ml) was added NaH (55%,
0.26 g, 5.96 mmol) at 0°C. After stirring for 5 min, S2 (prepared from
2-fluoro-5-nitrobenzoic acid, 1.5 g, 5.45 mmol) was added to the mixture
at 0 °C, and the resulting mixture was stirred overnight at RT. The
reaction mixture was quenched with water and the aqueous layer was
extracted with EtOAc. The combined organic layer was washed with brine,
dried over Na2SO4, filtered and concentrated in vacuo. The residue was
purified by flash column chromatography (hexane/EtOAc = 10/1). 21 (2.59
g, 100%) as a white solid. mp 109°C (recrystallized from hexane/EtOAc);
Rf 0.41 (Hexane/EtOAc=2/1); 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3) δ 8.81 (d, J= 2.7 Hz,
1H), 8.19 (dd, J= 9.2, 2.7 Hz, 1H), 7.48-7.44 (m, 2H), 7.39-7.34 (m, 4H),
6.58 (d, J=9.2, 1H), 5.42 (s, 2H) 5.08, (s, 2H), 3.99 (s, 3H), 3.62 (s,
3H), 3.42 (s, 3H); 13C NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3) δ 164.1, 163.5, 162.0, 153.8,
148.2, 141.8, 140.3, 135.4, 128.7, 128.52, 128.48, 127.8, 123.3, 123.0,
120.3, 114.9, 109.0, 99.9, 67.5, 58.0, 56.8, 52.6; IR (ATR) νmax 1726,
1709, 1702, 1519, 1275, 1103, 870, 746 cm-1 ; HRMS (ESI) calcd for
C25H22NO10ClNa [M+Na]+ 554.0812; found 554.0824.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Unexpected Diels-Alder/Carbonyl-ene Cascade toward the Biomimetic
Synthesis of Chloropupukeananin
