$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: In a typical procedure, 4-methoxythiophenol
(125 μL, 1.0 mmol) was added to a stirred suspension of Wang
4-fluoro-3-nitrobenzoate resin 2 (500 mg, 0.5 mmol) and potassium
carbonate (140 mg, 1.0 mmol) in dry DMF (5 mL). The reaction mixture was
maintained at 40°Cfor 16 h, filtered, washed sequentially with DMF,
CH2Cl2 and MeOH, and dried in vacuo. The resin was subsequently taken up
in 50% TFA/dry CH2Cl2 (3 mL) and mixed using an orbital shaker for 3 h.
The mixture was filtered and the residual resin was washed with CH2Cl2.
The filtrate and combined washings were evaporated to dryness. Entry: 4;
Producta: 4d; Purityb: 100%
