$DATUM 4-Acetamindo-4'-nitrodiphenyl Ether (3) 4-Acetamidophenol (1.51 g, 0.01
mol; 1), p-nitrochlorobenzene (1.57 g, 0.01 mol; 2), potassium carbonate
(3.2 g), and dimethylformamide (10.0 ml) were charged in a round-bottom
flask under stirring. The reaction mass was heated at 153 °C for 5 h. The
progress of the reaction was monitored by TLC. The reaction mass was
quenched in 40.0 ml deionized water. The product was isolated by
filtration and dried in an air oven at 50 °C. Purification of crude
product was done using ethanol and activated charcoal. Yield: 120% w/w.
4-Acetamindo-4'-nitrodiphenyl Ether (3), yield 120%. melting point: 151
to 153 °C. 1H NMR (CDCl3) (δ ppm): 8.4 (s, 1H), 8.17 (d, 2H, J = 7.8 Hz),
7.2 (d, 2H, J = 7.8 Hz), 7.3 (d, 2H, J = 7.0 Hz), 7.6 (d, 2H, J = 7.0
Hz), 2.22 (s, 3H).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
