$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM a) 4-ethyl-2-methoxy-1-(2-nitrophenoxy)benzene To a stirred solution of
2-fluoronitrobenzene (102 mg, 0.72 mmol) in dry Acetonitrile (20ml) was
added 4-Ethyl-2-methoxy phenol (109 mg, 0.72 mmol) in dry acetonitrile
(10ml) followed by potassium hydroxide (41 mg, 0.72 mmol). The reaction
mixture was heated to 800C and maintained for 2 hours. The solvent was
evaporated and taken in ethyl acetate (200ml).The organic layer was
washed with water followed by brine ,dried over anhydrous sodium sulfate
and concentrated under reduced pressure title compound used without
further purification. yield 205 mg, quantitative. MS (ES) m/e 274 (M+H)+.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM From Triclosan toward the Clinic: Discovery of Nonbiocidal, Potent FabI
Inhibitors for the Treatment of Resistant Bacteria
