$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM To a solution of N-propargyl piperidine 4-fluorophenylsulfone ethyl ester
22a 42 (3.00 g, 5.66 mmol) in DMF(10 mL) was added Cs2CO3 (4.7 g, 14.5
mmol) and 4-methoxyphenol (1.80 g, 14.5 mmol) and the solution was heated
to 95°C for 24 h. The solution was diluted with EtOAc and washed
successively with 1N NaOH and brine and then dried over MgSO4.
Concentration and chromatographic purification of the residue afforded
the methoxyphenyl ether 20a as a solid (2.67 g, 100%).
