$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Method A A solution of 1.0 equiv (typically
5.0 mmol) of amine in 50 mL of THF was added dropwise within 1 h at room
temperature to a magnetically stirred solution of 1.0 equiv of
1,5-difluoro-2,4-dinitrobenzene (DFDNB, 5.0 mmol) and 1.1 equiv of
diisopropylethylamine (DIPEA, 5.5 mmol) in 50 mL of THF. The reaction
mixture was continuously stirred for an additional 1 h at room
temperature. The solvent was evaporated, and water was added to
precipitate I1. The desired intermediate I1 was obtained in quantitative
yield after filtration and washed thoroughly with water. Method B DFDNB
(typically 5 mmol) was dissolved in acetone (20 mL), followed by addition
of 1.0 equiv of phenol (5 mmol) and 5.0 equiv of anhydrous K2CO3 (25
mmol). The reaction mixture was mechanically stirred at room temperature
for more than 5h until the total disappearance of DFDNB, as determined by
TLC. Undissolved excess K2CO3 was removed by filtration. Work up as
described above, the desired intermediate I1 was obtained in quantitative
yield. Intermediate I1 was not further purified and used directly for the
next reaction. Typical compound,
1-(3,5-dimethylphenoxy)-5-fluoro-2,4-dinitrobenzene, 1.49 g of yellow
powder, was obtained in 98% yield, with an HPLC purity >99%. ESI-MS: m/z
305.1 (M-H)-.
