$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM The pyridinyl ester 22b (5.66 mmol, 2.30 g), K2CO3 (9.0 mmol, 1.29 g),
4-hydroxyanisole (9 mmol, 1.12 g), and DMF(3mL) were heated at 75-80°C
for 24 h. The reaction was judged to be incomplete based on TLC, so an
additional 350 mg of base and 300 mg of the phenol were added, and
stirring was continued at ambient temperature for 2 d. The reaction was
then taken up in water (50 mL) and extracted with EtOAc (3 × 50 mL). The
combined organic layers were concentrated. The residue was purified by
chromatography, affording the diaryl ether 20b as an oil (2.85 g, 100%).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM more base and phenol added to reaction after first 24 h
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Orally Active MMP-1 Sparing α-Tetrahydropyranyl and α-Piperidinyl Sulfone
Matrix Metalloproteinase (MMP) Inhibitors with Efficacy in Cancer,
Arthritis, and Cardiovascular Disease
