$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM 2-(4-(4-(Butylcarbamoyl)-2-nitrophenoxy)-3-methoxyphenyl)-2-hydroxyacetic
acid N-butyl-4-chloro-3-nitrobenzamide (12.7 g, 49.5 mmol, 1 equiv.) and
DL-4-hydroxy-3-methoxymandelic acid (10 g, 50.5 mmol, 1.02 equiv.) were
dissolved in DMSO (50 mL). Cs2CO3 (34.7 g, 106.5 mmol, 2.15 equiv) was
added in portions and the reaction mixture was heated to 60°C for 2 h. A
sample of the reaction mixture was analyzed by hplc showing incomplete
conversion. An additional portion of Cs2CO3 (10 g) was added to the
reaction and the mixture was heated at 60°C for 2 h until complete
conversion was achieved. The reaction mixture was cooled to RT, water
(200 mL) was added and the pH was adjusted to 3 by the addition of 2N
HCl. The aqueous was extracted with EtOAc (2 x 200 mL). The combined
organic layers were washed with saturated NaCl solution, dried over
sodium sulfate, filtered and concentrated to give a yellow solid (20.4 g,
99%).
2-(4-(4-(Butylcarbamoyl)-2-nitrophenoxy)-3-methoxyphenyl)-2-hydroxyacetic
acid, yield20.4 g, 99%. Mp: 149.8-152.5°C 1H NMR (400 MHz, DMSO-d6) δ ppm
12.71 (br s, 1H), 8.62 (t, J=5.48 Hz, 1 H), 8.49 (d, J=1.96 Hz, 1 H),
8.04 (dd, J=8.71, 2.05 Hz, 1 H), 7.29 (s, 1 H), 7.21 (d, J=8.22 Hz, 1 H),
7.10 (d, J=8.22 Hz, 1 H), 6.86 (d, J=8.80 Hz, 1 H), 6.00 (br s, 1H), 5.09
(s, 1 H) 3.73 (s, 3 H), 3.26 (q, J=6.72 Hz, 2 H), 1.46 - 1.54 (m, 2 H),
1.27 - 1.37 (m, 2 H), 0.89 (t, J=7.34 Hz, 3 H). 13C NMR (101 MHz,
DMSO-d6) δ ppm 173.8, 163.5, 152.5, 150.5, 141.1, 139.3, 138.7, 133.6,
128.6, 124.4, 121.7, 119.6, 117.0, 111.9, 72.0, 55.9, 39.0, 31.1, 19.6,
13.7. IR (neat) 3312, 1729, 1621, 1528, 1275. HRMS calcd for C20H23N2O8
[M + H]+: 419.1449 found 419.1449
