$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Procedure for the Synthesis of
Coupling Products All reactions were carried out under air. Aryl halides
(1.0 mmol) were treated with phenol (1.0 mmol) in the presence of 0.1
mmol CuI, 0.2 mmol 1-(aaminobenzyl)- 2-naphthols and 2.0 equiv K2CO3 in
3mL DMSO at 120 °C for 24 h. The progress of the reaction was monitored
by gas chromatography (GC). After completion of the reaction, the
catalyst was filtered easily and the product was extracted with EtOAc,
The combined organic layers were dried over MgSO4 for 12 h. The solvent
was evaporated under reduced pressure and the desired product was
purified by flash chromatography on a silica-gel column using petroleum
ether= ethyl acetate (10:1). 2,4-dinitro-1-(m-tolyloxy)benzene (Table 3,
entry 4) 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3) δ: 8.88 (m, 1H, -CH-), 8.61 (m, 1H,
-CH-), 7.85 (m, J = 8.5 Hz, 1H, -CH-), 7.29 (m, 1H, -CH-), 7.16 (m, J =
8.0 Hz, 1H, -CH-), 6.95 (m, 1H, -CH-), 6.94 (m, 1H, -CH-), 2.34 (s, 3H,
-CH3). 13C NMR (101 MHz, CDCl3) δ: 158.9, 155.5, 141.9, 139.5, 138.1,
130.7, 128.3, 122.1, 121.0, 116.3, 115.0, 21.6. m/z: 274.06 (100.0%),
275.06 (15.0%), 276.06 (1.1%).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM green chemistry, Ullmann coupling, reusable catalyst, ligand prepared and
used
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Betti Base as an Efficient Ligand for Copper-Catalyzed Ullmann Coupling
of Phenol with Aryl Halides
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Yang, Li; Yang, Qichao; Shi, Jianxin; Wang, Yufang; Zhang, Mingjie
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Synthetic Communications (2014), 44(17), 2468-2477

$RFMT $RIREG SCHEME281 STEP1
