$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM 5-(4-Aminophenoxy)-2-nitroaniline (4). To a solution of 4-aminophenol
(5.0 g, 46 mmol) in DMF (120 mL) was slowly added 60% NaH (2.0 g, 50
mmol), followed by 5-chloro-2-nitroaniline (8.7 g). The mixture was
heated to 90 °C and stirred overnight. The reaction mixture was poured
onto aq NH4Cl to form a solid, which was collected by filtration, washed
with hexane, and dried to give 4 as a yellow solid (12.0 g, 99%): 1H NMR
(DMSO-d6 ) δ 5.11 (2H, s), 6.25 (2H, m), 6.62 (2H, d, J = 8.8 Hz), 6.82
(2H, d, J = 8.8 Hz), 7.45 (2H, s), 7.95 (d, 1H, J = 8.8 Hz); MS m/z 244
(M - 1).
