$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM 4-(3-Chlorophenoxy)benzoic Acid (25j). Prepared by heating a mixture of
KOH (199 mg, 3.0 mmol), 3-chlorophenol (337 μL, 3.2 mmol), and
4-fluorobenzonitrile (348 mg, 2.9 mmol) in DMF (1.5 mL) to 175 °C for 20
min in a sealed tube. Ether extraction gave the intermediate crude diaryl
ether, which was refluxed 12 h in 30% KOH aq. The resulting solution was
extracted with EtOAc, acidified, then extracted. 766 mg (99%) of the
desired acid (25j). 1H NMR (CDCl3) δ 8.10 (d, 2H, J = 8.7 Hz), 7.32 (t,
1H, J = 8.1 Hz), 7.21-7.16 (m, 1H), 7.08 (t, 1H, J = 2.0 Hz), 7.04 (d,
2H, J = 8.8 Hz), 7.00-6.95 (m, 1H). MS (ESI) m/z 247.3 (M-H)-.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM thermal (in stage 1), sealed tube used in stage 1, unspecified agent used
for pH adjustment in stage 3
