$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Procedure for the Palladium Catalyzed
Etherification of Aryl Halides with Sodium t-Butyldimethylsiloxide: A 4
mL vial was charged with 2-bromotoluene (86 mg, 0.50 mmol), Pd(dba)2
(14.0 mg, 0.025 mmol), Ph5FcP(t-Bu)2 (18.0 mg, 0.025 mmol) and sodium
tert-butyl-dimethylsiloxide (92 mg, 0.60 mmol). Anhydrous toluene (2 mL)
was added to the vial, and the vial was sealed witha cap containing a
PTFE septum and removed from the dry box. The reaction mixture was
stirred at room temperature for 48 h. The reaction solution was then
adsorbed onto silica gel, and the product was isolated by eluting with
ethyl acetate/hexanes (0 to 10% gradient). Yield 99%.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM catalyst formed in-situ
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
