$DATUM Methyl-4-(2-chloro-4-nitro-phenoxy)benzoate (12a): A mixture of methyl-4-
hydroxybenzoate (3.04 g, 20 mmol), 3-chloro-4-fluoro-nitrobenzene (3.51
g, 20 mmol) and K2CO3 (3.32 g, 24 mmol) in acetonitrile (50 mL) was
heated at reflux temperature during 3 hours. After cooling down, the
reaction mixture was poured into water, extracted with CH2Cl2, and the
combined organic layers dried over MgSO4. The title compound 12a was
obtained suitable for further use according to NMR analysis. Yellow
solid, yield 5.99 g, 98 %. 1H-NMR (300 MHz, CDCl3): δ 8.40 (d, J = 2.6
Hz, 1H), 8.11 (m, 3H), 7.09 (m, 3H), 3.93 (s, 3H) ppm; 13C-NMR (75 MHz,
CDCl3): δ 166.2, 158.9, 157.5, 143.8, 132.2, 127.1, 126.8, 126.2, 123.8,
119.1, 118.8, 52.4 ppm; mp 139 °C (Lit3: 123-124 °C); HRMS calcd for
[C14H10NO5Cl] 307.0248, found 307.0264.
