$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Synthesis of rac-P3 (Tribromophosphangulene). To a DMF (60 mL) solution
of 5 (1.507 g, 2.443 mmol) was added t-BuOK (823 mg, 7.33 mmol), and the
mixture was stirred at 140 °C for 23 h. After evaporation, distilled
water (100 mL) was added. The mixture was extracted with chloroform. The
combined organic phase was dried over MgSO4, and then evaporation gave a
crude brown powder. The crude products were washed with hexane. A pale
brown powder of rac-P3 (1.327 g, 98%). 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3) δ 7.24
(dd, J H-H = 8.8, J H-P = 5.2 Hz, 3H), 7.73 (d, J H-H = 8.8 Hz, 3H); 31P
NMR (162 MHz, CDCl3) δ -48.1 (s); 13C NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3) δ 107.9 (C, d,
J C-P = 7.3 Hz), 110.8 (C, d, J C-P = 106 Hz), 117.1 (CH, d, J C-P = 5.5
Hz), 137.0 (CH), 155.6 (C), 158.6 (C); MALDI-TOF MS m/z 556.77 [M+H]+.
Anal. Calcd for C18H6O4PBr3: C, 33.08; H, 1.26. Found: C, 33.25; H, 1.43.
